for close-set javelins
against him dart from bold hands
and burning torches, from which he trembles, hurrying though he is;

And as when an ass, going beside a field, has overpowered boys,
sluggish, on whom indeed many clubs round about are broken,
and crops, going in, the deep standing crop;

And Ajax at one time would be mindful of impetuous might,
turning back again, and would restrain the battle-lines
of the horse-taming Trojans;

and all he kept barring from marching to the swift ships,
but himself between Trojans and Achaeans he rushed,
taking his stand;

So spoke Eurypylus, struck; and they beside him
close together stood, the shields on their shoulders leaning,
spears holding up;

“Heavenly Menoetius’-son, made welcome to my heart,
now I think that around my knees will stand the Achaeans,
entreating;

and yellow honey, and beside it the meal of sacred barley,
and beside it a very fair cup, which from home the old man brought,
pierced through with golden studs;
